{
  "abstract": "We give a directed flag construction and a local characterization for cubic Lehman pairs. If binary square matrices $B,L$ satisfy $BL^{\\mathsf T}=J+2I$ and $B$ has row and column sum three, then $n=3q+1$ and the $3n$ flags of $B$ support complementary incidence factors with head size five and tail size $q$. These factors produce parameters $(9q+3,3q+4,q+8,q+3,q+2)$, recovering the known 30- and 84-vertex examples without a symmetry or self-duality hypothesis. Conversely, for the depth-two heads of any linear cubic incidence structure, every nonnegative integer tail of size $q$ whose own head intersection is zero and whose other head intersections are one or two is binary and satisfies $B(t+e_d)=\\mathbf1+2e_c$. Thus the tails uniquely force the Lehman mate; no tail regularity or inner product condition is needed in advance. Fixing one mate reduces the construction to matching colour classes in a cubic graph on $2q$ vertices. An exact integer enumeration of all 7,174,104 root colourings at $q=5$ excludes cubic excess-two pairs of order 16; order 13 is also excluded. Independent direct mate enumeration checks all smaller colourings, and literal positive graphs and complements are verified. This closes the stated flag class at 48 vertices, while unrestricted existence of $(48,19,13,8,7)$ and $(102,37,19,14,13)$ remains unresolved.",
